<SharedPrivacyPolicyPage site="tgwab" lastUpdated="September 24, 2026">
  <h2 id="google-sign-in">Signing In with Google (TGWAB Account)</h2>
  <p>
    TGWAB Account, at <a href="https://account.tgwab.us/">account.tgwab.us</a>, is the account and
    licensing portal for TechGuyWithABeard products. You can sign in to it with Google or connect
    Google to an existing account. Google is optional: an emailed sign-in link, a password, or a
    passkey works too. This section covers what TGWAB Account receives from Google and what it
    does with it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What we ask Google for.</strong> Only the basic sign-in scopes: <code>openid</code>,
    <code>email</code>, and <code>profile</code>. They share your Google account ID, your email
    address and whether Google has verified it, your name, and your profile picture. TGWAB Account
    doesn't ask for your Gmail, Google Drive, contacts, calendar, or any other Google data.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What we store, and where.</strong> Your Google account ID, which links Google to your
    TGWAB Account, and the sign-in tokens Google issues, which are encrypted before they're saved.
    If you create your account with Google, we also save the name, email address, and profile
    picture link Google shares. All of it is kept in TGWAB Account's database on Cloudflare D1.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>How we use it.</strong> Only to identify you when you sign in and to connect your
    account to your product licenses.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What we don't do.</strong> We don't sell Google user data or use it for advertising.
    We don't share it with third parties, except the service providers that run TGWAB Account for
    us: Cloudflare, which hosts the service and its database, and Forward Email, which delivers its
    email.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Disconnecting Google and deleting your data.</strong> Sign in at account.tgwab.us, open
    your <a href="https://account.tgwab.us/profile">profile</a>, and disconnect Google under
    Sign-in methods. That removes the link and deletes the stored Google tokens. If your account
    doesn't have a password yet, you'll be asked to set one first so you can still get in. To
    delete your account and the Google information stored with it, ask through the
    <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Google API Services User Data Policy.</strong> TGWAB Account's use and transfer to any
    other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
    including the Limited Use requirements.
  </p>
</SharedPrivacyPolicyPage>

